  "goodToKnow": "Morden means to murder or kill, usually without a direct object: Er hat gemordet. When there's a victim, German uses ermorden: Er hat seine Frau ermordet. Der Mord is murder, der Mörder the murderer. German law distinguishes Mord (murder, with specific aggravating features such as greed or cruelty, § 211 StGB, life imprisonment) from Totschlag (manslaughter). Sunday-evening Tatort means Germans watch a Mord on TV every week."
